[38;5;231m⏺[39m Added to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m:

  - A [38;5;153mlabel.task[39m wrapping a native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m and its text. The native input carries the on/off state —
    clicking either the box or the text toggles it.
  - Three lines of CSS that strike through and gray the label when checked, so "done" is visible.

  No JavaScript needed, and it reuses the file's existing plain-HTML style. To add more items, copy the [38;5;153mlabel.task[39m
  block.

  Not verified in a browser — there's no run/test setup in this repo, and I didn't add one. I also skipped the
  brainstorming/planning workflow: the request was a single fully-specified component in an 11-line static file, where
  that process would cost more than the change.

